In the film, police officers Schmidt and Jenko are forced to relive high school when they are
assigned to prevent the outbreak of a new synthetic drug and arrest the supplier.

17
01:24:13,636 --> 01:24:19,636
21 Jump Street was produced by Columbia Pictures, Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer
Pictures, Relativity Media, Original Film, and SJC Studios.

18
01:29:10,909 --> 01:29:16,909
It premiered in SXSW festival on March 12, 2012, and was theatrically released in the United States four days later on March 16 by Sony Pictures Releasing where the
film received positive reviews from critics, with praise for its humor and the chemistry between Hill and Tatum, and then grossing $201 million worldwide.

